    ['--name', 'yes', '—', 'Card name.'],
    ['--version', 'yes', '—', 'Card version (e.g. 1.0.0).'],
    ['--space', 'yes', '—', 'Card space.'],
    ['--label', 'no', '—', 'Label stored with the key row.'],
    ['--expires-in-seconds', 'no', '—', 'TTL override in seconds.'],
    ['--server', 'yes', 'WYRD_SERVER_URL', 'Wyrd server base URL.'],
    ['--token', 'yes', 'WYRD_ACCESS_TOKEN', 'Bearer access token with admin privileges.']
  ]}
/>

## wyrd eval run

Execute an Eval card. There are two source modes, and exactly one is required:

- **Live** — drive a running server against an agent endpoint: `--server` with
  `--agent-url`.
- **Local records** — score pre-collected observations: `--records`.

```bash
# Live run against an agent
wyrd eval run --eval ./eval.yaml \
  --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud --agent-url http://localhost:8080

# Offline scoring of recorded rows
wyrd eval run --eval ./eval.yaml --records ./observations.jsonl
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Flag', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Default' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['--eval', '(required)', 'Eval card filesystem path (JSON or YAML).'],
    ['--server', '—', 'Drive a remote server protocol router. Requires --agent-url.'],
    ['--agent-url', '—', 'Agent endpoint URL. Conflicts with --records.'],
    ['--records', '—', 'JSONL of pre-collected EvalRecordObservation rows. Conflicts with --server/--agent-url.'],
    ['--judge-mock', 'false', 'Deterministic judge — all LLM judge tasks return passed: true. Required if the spec has LLM judges and no provider is configured.'],
    ['--simulated-user', 'server', 'Who supplies unscripted user turns: server or client.'],
    ['--simulated-user-script', '—', 'JSONL of client-supplied user turns. Required when --simulated-user client.'],
    ['--baseline', '—', 'Baseline EvalResults JSON for comparison.'],
    ['--out', '—', 'Directory for local output artifacts (env WYRD_EVAL_OUT).'],
    ['--agent-timeout-secs', '60', 'Agent HTTP timeout in seconds.'],
    ['--fail-on-gate', 'true', 'Exit non-zero when the local pass gate fails.']
  ]}
/>

## wyrd principal revoke

Suspend a principal so it can mint no new token; tokens it already holds lapse
within five minutes. Requires an admin access token. The
principal ID is positional; `--kind` is required because IDs are unique only
within a kind.

```bash
wyrd principal revoke 3f9a...uuid --kind service --reason "key leaked" \
  --server https://acme.wyrd.cloud --token "$WYRD_ACCESS_TOKEN"
```

<DataTable
  columns={[
    { header: 'Argument', role: 'name' },
    { header: 'Required' },
    { header: 'Env' },
    { header: 'Meaning' }
  ]}
  rows={[
    ['<id>', 'yes', '—', 'Principal ID (UUID) to revoke.'],
    ['--kind', 'yes', '—', 'Principal kind: user, service, or agent.'],
    ['--reason', 'yes', '—', 'Audit reason for the revocation.'],
    ['--server', 'yes', 'WYRD_SERVER_URL', 'Wyrd server base URL.'],
    ['--token', 'yes', 'WYRD_ACCESS_TOKEN', 'Bearer access token with admin privileges.']
  ]}
/>

